    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe source code `'*'` triggers the same concealmeant as labels.\r\n\r\nFor example \r\n* label `*autocmd-pattern*` shows up as `autocmd-pattern`.\r\n* `'*'` inocrrectly shows up as `''`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nin `autocmd.txt` check the line with text `Note:  To match part of a path,`... with `set conceallevel=1`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nthe `'*'` to show up as a literal, not concealed.\n\n### Neovim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.9.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\n-\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n-\n\n### Installation\n\npackage manager",
